# XCU cal
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The whole utility is XSI-shaded and the layout of the calendar is
# unspecified. The tests read the output as words and look at the words that
# are decimal numbers up to 31: those are the day numbers of the month (the
# year in a heading is larger, the names are not numbers).

assertion  XCU.cal.001
anchor     utilities/cal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/cal.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       For month M and year Y, cal M Y writes each day number of the month
           once and no other number up to 31: 1 to 29 for 2 2024, 1 to 28 for
           2 2023, 1 to 30 for 4 2023, 1 to 31 for 1 2023 and 12 2023.
test       t/001-month-lengths.sh

assertion  XCU.cal.002
anchor     utilities/cal.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       Up to September 2, 1752 the Julian calendar applies, so February
           has 29 days in 1100, 1500, 1600 and 1700, and from September 14,
           1752 the Gregorian calendar, so February has 28 days in 1800 and
           1900 and 29 days in 2000.
test       t/002-julian-gregorian.sh

assertion  XCU.cal.003
anchor     utilities/cal.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       cal 9 1752 shows the days 1, 2 and 14 to 30 and none of 3 to 13.
test       t/003-september-1752.sh

assertion  XCU.cal.004
anchor     utilities/cal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/cal.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       A single operand is a year and gives all twelve months: for 2023,
           28 occurs twelve times, 29 and 30 eleven times and 31 seven times;
           cal 12 is the year 12 (twelve months, February with 29 days).
test       t/004-whole-year.sh

assertion  XCU.cal.005
anchor     utilities/cal.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       cal with no operands writes the calendar of the current month: the
           same day numbers as cal with that month and year as operands.
test       t/005-current-month.sh

assertion  XCU.cal.006
anchor     utilities/cal.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/cal.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       Operands outside the stated ranges (month 0 or 13, year 0 or
           10000, or a non-numeric operand) give a status above zero.
test       t/006-invalid-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.cal.007
anchor     utilities/cal.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/cal.html#STDERR
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       cal with valid operands exits with status zero and writes nothing
           to standard error.
test       t/007-status.sh
